WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.603
Coding Exercise 4 checks whether you understand ON
versus WHERE The

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:10.922
requirement says every patient must remain At the
same time only glucose

00:00:10.948 --> 00:00:16.202
lab rows should be allowed to match That means the
glucose condition

00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:22.228
should be part of the matching logic Complete the ON
clause Do

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:28.102
not add a WHERE condition that removes patients
without glucose tests Before

00:00:28.129 --> 00:00:32.987
running the query predict the shape of the result
Every patient ID

00:00:33.013 --> 00:00:37.526
should appear Some rows will have a glucose test ID
and value

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:43.951
Other patients will have NULL lab fields Use Run and
Check then

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:48.927
inspect both types of rows If only patients with
glucose tests remain

00:00:49.256 --> 00:00:55.071
review where you placed the test-name condition This
exercise is about preserving

00:00:55.084 --> 00:00:57.782
the population while restricting optional matches
